# Python Environment

**Applies to**: All Python code execution

## Strict Invariant: Fail-Fast (No Silent Tool Substitution)

**NEVER fall back to bare `python`, `python3`, `pip`, or ad-hoc `PYTHONPATH` hacks if `uv` fails.**

- When `uv` fails (due to missing virtualenvs, path mismatches, or sandbox permissions), the failure is an environment defect to diagnose or escalate—never an invitation to bypass `uv`.
- Silent tool substitution masks defects, violates determinism, and produces untracked environment drift.
- If a sandboxed agent environment blocks `uv` from accessing user-level installations (e.g. `~/.local/share/uv/python`), request sandbox bypass (`BypassSandbox: true`) or specify the runtime explicitly (`--python <path>`). Do not drop `uv`.

## Commands

| Action | Correct | Wrong |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Run script | `uv run [--project <path>] python script.py` | `python script.py`, `python3 script.py` |
| Run module | `uv run [--project <path>] python -m module` | `python -m module`, `python3 -m module` |
| Run tests | `uv run [--project <path>] pytest` | `pytest`, `python3 -m pytest`, `PYTHONPATH=... pytest` |
| Install package | `uv add package` (or `--project <path>`) | `pip install package` |
| Sync dependencies | `uv sync [--project <path>]` | `pip install -r requirements.txt` |
| Python REPL | `uv run [--project <path>] python` | `python` or `python3` |
| Run one-off tool | `uvx ruff check .` | `ruff check .` or `pipx run ruff` |
| Run inline script | Write to `/tmp/script.py`, then `uv run --project /abs/path python /tmp/script.py` | `uv run python -c "..."` (multiline or with comments) |
| Lint with ruff | `uv run --project /abs/path/to/service ruff check --fix file.py` | `uv run ruff check file.py`, `.venv/bin/ruff check file.py` |
| Format with ruff | `uv run --project /abs/path/to/service ruff format file.py` | `uv run ruff format file.py`, `.venv/bin/ruff format file.py` |

## Monorepo `--project` Requirement

When running commands from the repository root (or any directory other than the specific service/package directory), **always pass `--project <path-to-service-or-tests>`**.

Without `--project`:
- `uv` attempts to resolve `pyproject.toml` from the current working directory.
- If the repository root has no `pyproject.toml` (e.g. tests live in `tests/context-unit-tests/`), `uv` will fail to find installed tools (e.g. `pytest`) or dependencies.

## Why Bare Python Commands Fail

Bare `python`, `python3`, or `pytest` commands fail because:
- No virtual environment is activated
- Dependencies aren't isolated or available
- The wrong Python interpreter may be invoked

`uv run` automatically:
- Uses the project's virtual environment
- Ensures dependencies are installed and in sync
- Respects `.python-version`

## Project Setup

Each Python project must have:
- `pyproject.toml` with dependencies
- `.python-version` specifying Python version
- Virtual environment managed by `uv`

